# A host input holding a fact reference, recorded as one ExternalAssert
# ([RFCS.24]). Fixture 133_fcxt.
#
# The trace compares what each runtime does; the recording gates compare the
# two recordings atom by atom, read each with the other runtime, and replay
# each, so every case below is recorded and replayed in both.
#
# Handles: 0 the Inner, 1 MakeMid, 2 MakeOuter, 3 SendOuter, 4 DropMid,
# 5 the Mid copy and 6 the Outer the resend asserts, 7 MakeMid again,
# 8 the Holder.
# @spec [RFCS.24.1] [RFCS.24.2] [RFCS.24.3]
assert Inner v=10
assert MakeMid k=1
pump
assert MakeOuter n=1
pump
# Sent fact 0: the Outer, its Mid and its Inner inlined.
assert SendOuter n=1
pump
#
# 1. TWO DEEP, ONE COPY NEW AND ONE LIVE. The derived Mid is withdrawn; the
# Inner stays. The sent Outer comes back: its Inner copy is equal to the live
# Inner and is that fact (RFCS.23.7 step 1), its Mid copy is asserted new, and
# the Outer is received. One input step, one ExternalAssert listing the Mid and
# the Outer, innermost first (RFCS.24.3).
assert DropMid n=1
pump
resend 0
pump
#
# 2. A HOST RETRACT OF AN INLINED COPY, through the handle its ExternalAssert
# lists (RFCS.24.3): the recorded FactRetract names it, and a replay binds it.
retract 5
pump
#
# 3. A DIRECT HOST ASSERT REFERRING TO A DERIVED FACT. A Mid is derived again
# and the Holder names it: one ExternalAssert, the Holder with the Mid and its
# Inner inlined (RFCS.24.1). On replay the copies resolve to the re-derived Mid
# and the live Inner, and the Holder alone is asserted.
assert MakeMid k=2
pump
assert Holder h=1 m=@Mid
pump
